From 5f55fe5848e9c23a35b2772f306404840b6cef6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Anthropic)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 07:54:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove role concept; split /platform into stats dashboard +
 client management

- Drop the Role enum/field entirely (User model, session payload, signup/login,
  VIEWER-gated API checks, canEdit plumbing in Goals/Allocation/Accounts
  client components). Every household login now has full read/write access
  to its own data, consistent with the one-login-per-household model.
- Delete app/api/platform/users/[userId]/role/route.ts and the role dropdown
  in PlatformClientsClient.
- Rewrite app/platform/page.tsx as a real stats dashboard (new signups,
  clients by location, Free vs Subscription split) instead of the client
  list.
- Move the client list to the new app/platform/clients/page.tsx.
- Rename the sidebar's 'User Management' link to 'Client Management',
  fixing the 404 (the route now exists).
